{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0397"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__pop-rock.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",610],["+","CBGB also launched Blondie, formed in 1974 by the guitarist Chris Stein and the platinum-blonde singer Debbie Harry, a former waitress at Max's Kansas City who has fronted the band ever since. Their self-titled debut appeared in December 1976, and the group's mix of punk attitude, girl-group pop and later disco made it the New York scene's biggest commercial success, with „Heart of Glass“ topping the charts in 1979.\n\n"],["=",280],["+","Blondie | Blondie | December 1976 |\n| "],["=",60],["-","Five"],["+","Six"],["=",7],["-","less"],["+","barely"],["=",1],["-","than "],["=",17]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",558],["+","Aus dem CBGB kam auch Blondie, 1974 vom Gitarristen Chris Stein und der platinblonden Sängerin Debbie Harry gegründet, einer früheren Kellnerin im Max's Kansas City, die die Band seither anführt. Das nach der Band benannte Debüt erschien im Dezember 1976, und die Mischung aus Punk-Haltung, Girlgroup-Pop und später Disco machte die Gruppe zum größten kommerziellen Erfolg der New Yorker Szene – „Heart of Glass“ stand 1979 an der Spitze der Charts.\n\n"],["=",278],["+","Blondie | Blondie | Dezember 1976 |\n| "],["=",60],["-","Fünf"],["+","Sechs"],["=",7],["-","weniger"],["+","kaum"],["=",1],["-","als "],["=",17]]}]},
